[Bounty: $400] Script API Custom Slash Command Throws Unhandled Startup Exception

### Bug Description
We are migrating our administration scripts to the modern Bedrock Script API (`@minecraft/server` 2.x). 

When registering custom slash commands (e.g. `/inspect`), our script crashes during world load with:
```text
[Scripting][ERROR] TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'registerCommand')
    at initCommands (scripts/commands.ts:12:20)
```

### Current Implementation (`scripts/commands.ts`)
```typescript
import { world, system } from '@minecraft/server';

export function registerCustomCommands() {
  system.runInterval(() => {
    // Attempting registration once world ticks
    world.beforeEvents.chatSend.subscribe((event) => {
      if (event.message.startsWith('/inspect')) {
        event.cancel = true;
        // handle logic
      }
    });
  });
}
```

