> **Severity:** Medium · **Component:** `paraloom-wallet` · **Reward tier:** up to $150 USDC
> **Tested:** wallet `main` @ `1e79eec8fbe99cd7e1381f6971c855bdce883d41` · local mocks only · no live chain touched

## Summary

`depositSpl()` persists a re-shield note at submission time (correctly preserving the random blinding), but then **ignores a real confirmation timeout**.

`confirmBySignatureStatus()` returns `false` when a submitted signature is never observed before its 90-second deadline. The caller does this:

```ts
await confirmBySignatureStatus(connection, signature)
return result
```

The boolean is discarded, so a transaction that was submitted but never landed is returned as a successful `DepositResult`.

That is especially harmful in the private-swap re-shield path because the `onSubmitted` callback has already persisted the note into the wallet's confirmed-looking local note set.

